    "Proposed Hindi patterns for src/data/claims-lint.json (patterns.hi of each rule) and src/data/keyword-map.json (seOwned.hi, seOwnedLead.hi, reserved.G1.hi). Not merged: the owner decides (M3 hi translator, 2026-10-06).",
    "Coverage: every claims-lint rule with per-locale patterns and no hi key yet (25 rules, hype included: it has per-locale keys besides '*'). Skipped: selection-translate and jargon (already have hi), io-home and engine-claim ('*' only).",
    "Matching as in the validator: case-insensitive with the u flag, on the rendered text. Since bb689eb \\w, \\W and \\b in these data files cover letters, marks and digits of every script, so \\b works around Devanagari words (a word may end in a vowel sign, which is \\p{M}, not \\p{L}). Nukta letters are written as base + U+093C (NFC); the hi glossary bans the precomposed forms U+0958–U+095F in the copy, so one spelling is enough. ज़/फ़ in a pattern are written 'ज़?' / 'फ़?' (optional nukta) so a spelling without the nukta is caught too.",
    "Tested on the hi copy (0 hits outside the rules' exempt keys) and on the counter-examples listed in docs/redesign-2026/ops/m3/hi-qa.md, appendix A."
  ],
